    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--1\"><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><p><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">幽邃盲族由普通人類退化而成。它們的祖先由於歷代崇拜跟隨奪心魔在幽暗地域中潛伏過活，而逐漸轉變成盲目而魁梧的食人怪物。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:黑體\"><em><strong>卑微的信徒Debased Cultists。</strong></em></span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">奪心魔帝國的版圖曾經延伸至許多相異的世界，並奴役了無數的種族。這些被奴役者中從不缺乏人類族羣的存在。奪心魔們用險惡的能力控制族羣高階祭司的思想，讓族羣的領導者們逐漸轉變信仰，最終崇拜靈吸怪們爲瀆神的造物主。<br />隨着時間的推移，這些被奴役的人類自發形成了狂熱的食人文化，並把奪心魔食腦的行爲尊爲聖餐儀式。靈吸怪們順勢命令崇拜者前去綁架其他的智能生物作祭品，然後在吸食受害者的大腦後，讓信徒們處理這些失去生命的屍體。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:黑體\"><em><strong>盲眼獵人Blind Hunters。</strong></em></span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">奪心魔的統治崩潰後，它們的崇拜者隨即失去了靠山。曾經遭受獵殺的生物們對它們圍追堵截，繼而引發了無數的戰爭。殘存的信衆最後一起逃向了幽暗地域，一個有如其靈吸怪神明神域一樣的地方。在後來的歲月裏，世代的無光生活使信徒們被逼學習依賴其他感官生存。久而久之，它們的眼睛和眼瞼漸漸枯萎封閉，只留下皮膚覆蓋着的空眼眶。<br />幽邃盲族的耳朵可以聽清遙遠石路上的腳步與低語，然後用低到其他類人生物都無法聽到的聲量進行交流。汗水和血肉的氣味會喚起它們的飢餓感，並促使它們如尋血犬般追蹤源頭。爲了增強自己的感官，幽邃盲族在巢穴範圍之外佈滿血污、糞堆和獵物內臟。當入侵者經過這些地區時，沾染上的這些污濁氣味可以讓幽邃盲族迅速發現對方的存在。<br />對大多數生物而言，失明是一種嚴重的活動障礙。但幽邃盲族由於擁有其他的敏銳感官，視覺反而成爲一種多餘的干擾。而幽邃盲族現有的感官結構足以讓它們在獵殺時更加無所畏懼。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:黑體\"><em><strong>無盡的戰爭Endless War。</strong></em></span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">幽邃盲族至今仍崇拜着奪心魔，並想盡辦法爲它們服務。而那些驅使它們逃往地下的戰爭也依然纏繞不休。然而它們仍時常爲靈吸怪主子們綁架獵物，併爲此返回到地表世界的戰爭中，完全沒有要結束這種惡性循環的想法。</span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"font-family:'Noto Sans SC'\">The degenerate subterranean grimlocks were once human, but their worship of the mind flayers over generations of prowling the Underdark transformed them into blind, monstrous cannibals long ago.</span></p><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Debased Cultists\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Debased Cultists.</span> The empire of the mind flayers once spread across many worlds, enslaving countless races. Among those were human cultures whose high priests the mind flayers subverted using their insidious powers of thought control. Those leaders gradually turned the faiths of their followers toward the illithids, which they worshiped as blasphemous deities.</p><p>Over time, the rituals of these enslaved humans created fervent cannibal cults that regarded the brain eating of the mind flayers as a holy sacrament. The illithids commanded their worshipers to abduct other sentient creatures to be sacrificed. After the victims' brains had been consumed, the mind flayers gave the lifeless bodies to the cultists.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Blind Hunters\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Blind Hunters.</span> When the rule of the mind flayers crumbled, their cults faced constant warfare from their enemies, the same creatures that had once been their victims. The cults fled into the Underdark domains of their illithid gods. Over generations in that lightless realm, the cultists learned to rely on their other senses for survival. In time, their eyes withered away and eyelids sealed, leaving only covered eye sockets behind.</p><p>A grimlock's ears prick up at the faintest footfall or whisper echoing down stone passageways. It can speak in tones too low for most other humanoids to hear. The odors of sweat, flesh, and blood awaken its hunger, and it can track by such scents like a bloodhound. To enhance their senses, grimlocks leave trails of blood, piles of dung, or the viscera of slain prey in places far from their lairs. When intruders pass through those areas, they carry the foul scents with them, warning the grimlocks of their approach.</p><p>For most creatures, blindness is an enormous hindrance. For a grimlock with its other heightened senses, sightlessness is a boon. A grimlock isn't fooled by visual illusions or misperceptions. It is fearless as it stalks prey.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Endless War\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Endless War.</span> Grimlocks still venerate the mind flayers, serving them whenever possible. Grimlocks also recall the war in which they were driven underground. To them, it has never ended. They continue to return to the surface world to abduct captives for their illithid masters.</p></div></div></div>",
        "public": ""
      },
